msgid ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR Bands (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere radiances in six solar reflective channels at 500 m "
"resolution: S1 (0.555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0.659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/cloud flagging), S4 (1.375 µm, cirrus detection), S5 "
"(1.61 µm, ice/snow/vegetation), and S6 (2.25 µm, vegetation state). Each "
"band is available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle "
"observation of land and ocean surfaces. The L1B product contains "
"geolocated, calibrated radiances produced by signal calibration, "
"re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# Bandaí VIS/SWIR SLSTR (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Gabhann Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) "
"radaíochtaí Barr an Atmaisféir i sé chainéal fhrithchaitheacha gréine ag "
"taifeach 500 m: S1 (0.555 µm, plandúlacht/aeróisil), S2 (0.659 µm, "
"NDVI/aeróisil), S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/brath scamall), S4 (1.375 µm, brath "
"cioras), S5 (1.61 µm, oighear/sneachta/plandúlacht), agus S6 (2.25 µm, "
"staid plandúlachta). Tá gach banda ar fáil i radharcanna nadir agus "
"claonta, rud a chumasaíonn breathnóireacht dé-uillinne ar dhromchlaí talún "
"agus aigéin. Tá radaíochtaí geoshuite, calabraithe sa táirge L1B a "
"tháirgtear trí chalabrú comharthaí, athghrídeáil, agus brath scamall.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# SLSTR Thermal Infrared Bands (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere brightness temperatures in three thermal infrared "
"channels at 1 km resolution: S7 (3.74 µm, sea/land surface temperature and "
"fire detection), S8 (10.85 µm, sea/land surface temperature and fire "
"detection), and S9 (12.0 µm, sea/land surface temperature). Each band is "
"available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle observation for "
"improved atmospheric correction and surface temperature retrieval. The L1B "
"product contains geolocated, calibrated brightness temperatures produced by "
"signal calibration, re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# Bandaí Infridhearg Teirmeach SLSTR (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Gabhann Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) "
"teochtaí gile Barr an Atmaisféir i dtrí chainéal infridhearg teirmeach ag "
"taifeach 1 km: S7 (3.74 µm, teocht dromchla farraige/talún agus brath "
"tine), S8 (10.85 µm, teocht dromchla farraige/talún agus brath tine), agus "
"S9 (12.0 µm, teocht dromchla farraige/talún). Tá gach banda ar fáil i "
"radharcanna nadir agus claonta, rud a chumasaíonn breathnóireacht "
"dé-uillinne chun ceartú atmaisféir agus aisghabháil teochta dromchla a "
"fheabhsú. Tá teochtaí gile geoshuite, calabraithe sa táirge L1B a "
"tháirgtear trí chalabrú comharthaí, athghrídeáil, agus brath scamall.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal IR fire emission bands\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) has two "
"dedicated channels (F1 and F2) that aim to detect Land Surface Temperature "
"(LST). F2 Channel, with a central wavelength of 10854 nm measures in the "
"thermal infrared, or TIR. It is very useful for fire and high temperature "
"event monitoring at 1 km resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"
msgstr ""
"# Bandaí astaithe tine infridhearg teirmeach\n"
"\n"
"Tá dhá chainéal tiomnaithe (F1 agus F2) ag Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface "
"Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) a bhfuil sé mar aidhm acu Teocht Dromchla "
"Talún (LST) a bhrath. Tomhaiseann Cainéal F2, le tonnfhad lárnach de 10854 "
"nm, san infridhearg teirmeach, nó TIR. Tá sé an-úsáideach chun "
"monatóireacht a dhéanamh ar thine agus ar imeachtaí ardteochta ag taifeach "
"1 km.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"

msgid ""
"# Cloud base height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud base measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Airde bhonn an scamaill\n"
"\n"
"Airde bhonn an scamaill arna tomhas i méadair (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud base pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud base in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Brú bhonn an scamaill\n"
"\n"
"Brú arna thomhas ag bonn an scamaill i bPascal (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Effective radiometric cloud fraction\n"
"\n"
"Effective radiometric cloud fraction represents the portion of the Earth's "
"surface covered by clouds, divided by the total surface. Clouds have "
"shielding, albedo, and in-cloud absorption effects on trace gas retrieval. "
"The effective radiometric cloud fraction is an important parameter to "
"correct these effects."
msgstr ""
"# Codán éifeachtach raidiméadrach scamall\n"
"\n"
"Léiríonn an codán éifeachtach raidiméadrach scamall an chuid de dhromchla "
"an Domhain atá clúdaithe ag scamaill, roinnte ar an dromchla iomlán. Bíonn "
"éifeachtaí scáthaithe, albedo, agus ionsú laistigh den scamall ag scamaill "
"ar aisghabháil gás rianaithe. Is paraiméadar tábhachtach é an codán "
"éifeachtach raidiméadrach scamall chun na héifeachtaí seo a cheartú."

msgid ""
"# Cloud optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"The cloud thickness is a key parameter to characterise optical properties "
"of clouds. It is a measure of how much sunlight passes through the cloud to "
"reach Earth's surface. The higher a cloud's optical thickness, the more "
"sunlight the cloud is scattering and reflecting. Dark blue shows where "
"there are low cloud optical thickness values and red shows larger cloud "
"optical thickness."
msgstr ""
"# Tiús optúil scamaill\n"
"\n"
"Is paraiméadar tábhachtach é tiús an scamaill chun airíonna optúla scamall "
"a shainiú. Is tomhas é ar cé mhéad solais ghréine a théann trí chuid den "
"scamall chun dromchla an Domhain a bhaint amach. Dá airde tiús optúil "
"scamaill, is mó solas gréine a scaipeann agus a fhrithchaitheann an "
"scamall. Léiríonn gorm dorcha na háiteanna a bhfuil luachanna ísle tiús "
"optúil scamaill iontu agus léiríonn dearg tiús optúil scamaill níos mó."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud top measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Airde bharr an scamaill\n"
"\n"
"Airde bharr an scamaill arna tomhas i méadair (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud top in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Brú bharr an scamaill\n"
"\n"
"Brú arna thomhas ag barr an scamaill i bPascal (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal band 10\n"
"\n"
"This thermal visualization is based on band 10 (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). At the central wavelength of 10895 nm it measures in the thermal "
"infrared, or TIR. Instead of measuring the temperature of the air, like "
"weather stations do, band 10 reports on the ground itself, which is often "
"much hotter. Thermal band 10 is useful in providing surface temperatures "
"and is collected with a 100-meter resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."
msgstr ""
"# Banda teirmeach 10\n"
"\n"
"Tá an amharcléiriú teirmeach seo bunaithe ar bhanda 10 (is réigiún den "
"speictream leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le braiteoir satailíte "
"an Domhan a léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla). Ag an tonnfhad lárnach 10895 nm, "
"tomhaiseann sé san infridhearg teirmeach, nó TIR. In ionad teocht an aeir a "
"thomhas, mar a dhéanann stáisiúin aimsire, tuairiscíonn banda 10 ar an "
"talamh féin, a bhíonn go minic i bhfad níos teo. Tá banda teirmeach 10 "
"úsáideach chun teochtaí dromchla a sholáthar agus bailítear é le taifeach "
"100 méadar.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference vegetation index is a simple, but effective index "
"for quantifying green vegetation. It is a measure of the state of "
"vegetation health based on how plants reflect light at certain wavelengths. "
"The value range of the NDVI is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDVI (values "
"approaching -1) correspond to water. Values close to zero (-0.1to 0.1) "
"generally correspond to barren areas of rock, sand, or snow. Low, positive "
"values represent shrub and grassland (approximately 0.2 to 0.4), while high "
"values indicate temperate and tropical rainforests (values approaching 1).\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Plandúlachta (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Is innéacs simplí ach éifeachtach é an t-innéacs difríochta normalaithe "
"plandúlachta chun plandúlacht ghlas a chainníochtú. Is tomhas é ar staid "
"sláinte na plandúlachta bunaithe ar an gcaoi a bhfrithchaitheann plandaí "
"solas ag tonnfhaid áirithe. Is é -1 go 1 raon luachanna an NDVI. "
"Freagraíonn luachanna diúltacha NDVI (luachanna ag druidim le -1) d'uisce. "
"Freagraíonn luachanna gar do nialas (-0.1 go 0.1) go ginearálta do "
"limistéir loma de charraig, gaineamh, nó sneachta. Léiríonn luachanna "
"dearfacha ísle tor agus féarthalamh (thart ar 0.2 go 0.4), agus léiríonn "
"luachanna arda foraoisí báistí measartha agus trópaiceacha (luachanna ag "
"druidim le 1).\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"The enhanced vegetation index (EVI) is an 'optimized' vegetation index as "
"it corrects for soil background signals and atmospheric influences. It is "
"very useful in areas of dense canopy cover. The range of values for EVI is "
"-1 to 1, with healthy vegetation generally around 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More infos [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) "
"and [here.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Feabhsaithe Plandúlachta (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"Is innéacs plandúlachta 'optamaithe' é an t-innéacs feabhsaithe "
"plandúlachta (EVI) toisc go gceartaíonn sé do chomharthaí cúlra ithreach "
"agus do thionchair atmaisféir. Tá sé an-úsáideach i limistéir le clúdach "
"tiubh clúdaigh. Is é -1 go 1 raon luachanna an EVI, agus plandúlacht "
"shláintiúil thart ar 0.20 go 0.80 go ginearálta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) agus "
"[anseo.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"

msgid ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI) is a vegetation index "
"that minimizes the effects of atmospheric scattering. It is most useful for "
"regions with high content of atmospheric aerosol (fog, dust, smoke, air "
"pollution). The range for an ARVI is -1 to 1 where green vegetation "
"generally falls between values of 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Plandúlachta atá Frithsheasmhach in aghaidh an Atmaisféir (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"Is innéacs plandúlachta é an tInnéacs Plandúlachta atá Frithsheasmhach in "
"aghaidh an Atmaisféir (ARVI) a íoslaghdaíonn éifeachtaí scaipthe "
"atmaisféir. Tá sé is úsáidí i réigiúin a bhfuil ábhar ard aeróisil "
"atmaisféir iontu (ceo, deannach, deatach, truailliú aeir). Is é -1 go 1 an "
"raon d'ARVI, agus titeann plandúlacht ghlas go ginearálta idir luachanna "
"0.20 go 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) agus "
"[anseo.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-"
"your-vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index is similar to Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) but is used in areas where vegetative cover is low "
"(< 40%). The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil "
"brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and "
"near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is helpful when analysing young "
"crops, arid regions with sparse vegetation and exposed soil surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Plandúlachta Coigeartaithe d'Ithir (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"Is cosúil an tInnéacs Plandúlachta Coigeartaithe d'Ithir leis an Innéacs "
"Difríochta Normalaithe Plandúlachta (NDVI) ach úsáidtear é i limistéir ina "
"bhfuil clúdach plandúlachta íseal (< 40%). Is teicníocht chlaochlaithe é an "
"t-innéacs a íoslaghdaíonn tionchar gile na hithreach ar innéacsanna "
"plandúlachta speictreacha a bhaineann le tonnfhaid dhearga agus "
"gar-infridheirg (NIR). Tá an t-innéacs úsáideach agus barra óga, réigiúin "
"thirim le plandúlacht tanaí agus dromchlaí ithreach nochta á n-anailísiú.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) agus "
"[anseo.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-"
"your-vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Anthocyanins are pigments common in higher plants, causing their red, blue "
"and purple coloration. They provide valuable information about the "
"physiological status of plants, as they are considered indicators of "
"various types of plant stresses. The reflectance of anthocyanin is highest "
"around 550nm. However, the same wavelengths are reflected by chlorophyll as "
"well. To isolate the anthocyanins, the 700nm spectral band, that reflects "
"only chlorophyll and not anthocyanins, is subtracted.\n"
"\n"
"To correct for leaf density and thickness, the near infrared spectral band "
"(in the recommended wavelengths of 760-800nm), which is related to leaf "
"scattering, is added to the basic ARI index. The new index is called "
"modified ARI or mARI (also ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI values for the examined trees in [this original "
"article](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) ranged "
"in values from 0 to 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Frithchaitheachta Antocyanin Athraithe (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Is pigmintí iad antocyanin atá coitianta i bplandaí ardchéime, a thugann a "
"ndath dearg, gorm agus corcra dóibh. Soláthraíonn siad faisnéis luachmhar "
"faoi stádas fiseolaíoch plandaí, mar go meastar gur táscairí iad ar "
"chineálacha éagsúla strus plandaí. Bíonn frithchaitheacht antocyanin ar a "
"airde timpeall 550nm. Ach frithchaitheann clóraifil na tonnfhaid chéanna "
"freisin. Chun na hantocyanin a leithlisiú, baintear an banda speictreach "
"700nm, a fhrithchaitheann clóraifil amháin agus nach bhfrithchaitheann "
"antocyanin, den toradh.\n"
"\n"
"Chun ceartú a dhéanamh do dhlús agus do thiús duilleoga, cuirtear an banda "
"speictreach gar-infridheirg (sna tonnfhaid mholta 760-800nm), a bhaineann "
"le scaipeadh duilleoige, leis an mbunínnéacs ARI. Tugtar ARI athraithe nó "
"mARI (ARI2 freisin) ar an innéacs nua.\n"
"\n"
"Bhí luachanna mARI do na crainn a ndearnadh scrúdú orthu sa [bhunalt "
"seo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) idir 0 agus "
"8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"

msgid ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"The Green city script aims to raise awareness of green areas in cities "
"around the world. The script takes into account the Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) and true color wavelengths; it separates built up "
"areas from vegetated ones, making it useful for detecting urban areas. "
"Built up areas are displayed in grey and vegetation is displayed in green.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"
msgstr ""
"# Script Chathair Ghlas\n"
"\n"
"Tá sé mar aidhm ag an script Cathair ghlas feasacht a ardú ar limistéir "
"ghlasa i gcathracha ar fud an domhain. Cuireann an script an tInnéacs "
"Difríochta Normalaithe Plandúlachta (NDVI) agus tonnfhaid fíordhatha san "
"áireamh; scarann sé limistéir thógtha ó limistéir phlandaithe, rud a "
"fhágann go bhfuil sé úsáideach chun limistéir uirbeacha a bhrath. "
"Taispeántar limistéir thógtha i liath agus taispeántar plandúlacht i nglas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"The Urban Classified script aims to detect built up areas by separating "
"them from barren ground, vegetation and water. Areas with a high moisture "
"content are returned in blue; areas indicating built up areas are returned "
"in white; vegetated areas are returned in green; everything else indicates "
"barren ground and is displayed in brown colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/"
")"
msgstr ""
"# Script Aicmithe Uirbeach\n"
"\n"
"Tá sé mar aidhm ag an script Aicmithe Uirbeach limistéir thógtha a bhrath "
"trína scaradh ó thalamh loma, plandúlacht agus uisce. Tugtar limistéir a "
"bhfuil ábhar tais ard iontu ar ais i ngorm; tugtar limistéir a léiríonn "
"limistéir thógtha ar ais i mbán; tugtar limistéir phlandaithe ar ais i "
"nglas; léiríonn gach rud eile talamh loma agus taispeántar é i ndathanna "
"donna.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_"
"classified/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"This script, made by Leo Tolari, combines true color visualization with "
"near infrared (NIR) and shortwave infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. The script "
"highlights urban areas better than true color, while still looking natural.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"
msgstr ""
"# Script Datha Infridhearg Talún Uirbigh\n"
"\n"
"Comhcheanglaíonn an script seo, a rinne Leo Tolari, amharcléiriú fíordhatha "
"le tonnfhaid gar-infridheirg (NIR) agus infridhearg gearrthonnach (SWIR). "
"Aibhsíonn an script limistéir uirbeacha níos fearr ná fíordhath, agus í fós "
"ag breathnú nádúrtha.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"

msgid ""
"# NDMI for Moisture Stress\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) for moisture stress can be "
"used to detect irrigation. For all the index values above 0, knowing the "
"land use and land cover, it is possible to determine whether irrigation has "
"taken place. Knowing the type of crop grown (e.g. citrus crops), it is "
"possible to identify whether irrigation is being effective or not during "
"the crucial growing summer season, as well as find out if some parts of the "
"farm are being under or over-irrigated.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"
msgstr ""
"# NDMI do Strus Taise\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir an tInnéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Taise (NDMI) do strus taise a "
"úsáid chun uisciú a bhrath. I gcás gach luach innéacs os cionn 0, agus "
"úsáid talún agus clúdach talún ar eolas, is féidir a chinneadh ar tharla "
"uisciú. Agus cineál an bharr a fhástar (m.sh. barra citris) ar eolas, is "
"féidir a aithint an bhfuil uisciú éifeachtach nó nach bhfuil le linn "
"shéasúr tábhachtach fáis an tsamhraidh, chomh maith le fáil amach an bhfuil "
"codanna den fheirm á n-uisciú róbheag nó rómhór.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference moisture Index (NDMI) is used to determine "
"vegetation water content and monitor droughts. The value range of the NDMI "
"is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDMI (values approaching -1) correspond to "
"barren soil. Values around zero (-0.2 to 0.4) generally correspond to water "
"stress. High, positive values represent high canopy without water stress "
"(approximately 0.4 to 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Taise (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"Úsáidtear an t-innéacs difríochta normalaithe taise (NDMI) chun ábhar uisce "
"plandúlachta a chinneadh agus triomaigh a mhonatóiriú. Is é -1 go 1 raon "
"luachanna an NDMI. Freagraíonn luachanna diúltacha NDMI (luachanna ag "
"druidim le -1) d'ithir loma. Freagraíonn luachanna timpeall nialas (-0.2 go "
"0.4) go ginearálta do strus uisce. Léiríonn luachanna arda dearfacha "
"clúdach ard gan strus uisce (thart ar 0.4 go 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. Values of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller "
"values. Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Uisce (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Is é an t-innéacs difríochta normalaithe uisce an ceann is oiriúnaí do "
"mhapáil comhlachtaí uisce. Tá luachanna comhlachtaí uisce níos mó ná 0.5. "
"Tá luachanna níos lú ag plandúlacht. Tá luachanna dearfacha idir nialas "
"agus 0.2 ag gnéithe tógtha.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) and [here.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh datha bhréagaigh\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann comhshuíomh datha bhréagaigh tonnfhad amháin nach bhfuil "
"infheicthe ar a laghad chun an Domhan a léiriú. Tá an comhshuíomh datha "
"bhréagaigh a úsáideann bandaí gar-infridheirg, dearg agus glas "
"an-choitianta (is réigiún den speictream leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is "
"féidir le braiteoir satailíte an Domhan a léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla). "
"Úsáidtear an comhshuíomh datha bhréagaigh go coitianta chun dlús agus "
"sláinte plandaí a mheas, ós rud é go bhfrithchaitheann plandaí solas "
"gar-infridheirg agus solas glas, agus go n-ionsúnn siad solas dearg. Bíonn "
"cathracha agus talamh nochta liath nó buí-donn, agus bíonn uisce le "
"feiceáil gorm nó dubh.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) agus [anseo.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
