"gar-infridheirg agus solas glas, agus go n-ionsúnn siad solas dearg. Bíonn "
"cathracha agus talamh nochta liath nó buí-donn, agus bíonn uisce le "
"feiceáil gorm nó dubh.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/)."

msgid ""
"# True color optimized\n"
"\n"
"This optimized True color script uses the visible light bands red, green "
"and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting "
"in a product with natural colours that represents the Earth as humans would "
"naturally see it. The visualisation uses highlight compression and improves "
"the contrast and color vividness through minor contrast and saturation "
"enhancement.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info for "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) "
"and for "
"[L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."
msgstr ""
"# Fíordhath optamaithe\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an script optamaithe Fíordhath seo na bandaí solais infheicthe "
"dearg, glas agus gorm sna cainéil dhatha chomhfhreagracha dearg, glas agus "
"gorm, rud a fhágann táirge le dathanna nádúrtha a léiríonn an Domhan mar a "
"d'fheicfeadh daoine go nádúrtha é. Úsáideann an t-amharcléiriú comhbhrú "
"buaicphointí agus feabhsaíonn sé codarsnacht agus bríomhaireacht datha trí "
"fheabhsú beag codarsnachta agus sáithiúcháin.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais le haghaidh "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) "
"agus le haghaidh "
"[L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum. Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. Landsat 8-9 has 11 bands. True color composite uses visible light "
"bands red, green and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color "
"channels, resulting in a natural colored product, that is a good "
"representation of the Earth as humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh fíordhatha\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir le braiteoirí a iompraíonn satailítí an Domhan a léiriú i "
"réigiúin éagsúla den speictream leictreamaighnéadach. Tugtar banda ar gach "
"réigiún sa speictream. Tá 11 bhanda ag Landsat 8-9. Úsáideann comhshuíomh "
"fíordhatha bandaí solais infheicthe dearg, glas agus gorm sna cainéil "
"dhatha chomhfhreagracha dearg, glas agus gorm, rud a fhágann táirge datha "
"nádúrtha, a léiríonn an Domhan go maith mar a d'fheicfeadh daoine go "
"nádúrtha é.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum . Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. True color composite uses visible light bands red, green and blue in "
"the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting in a "
"natural colored product, that is a good representation of the Earth as "
"humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh fíordhatha\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir le braiteoirí a iompraíonn satailítí an Domhan a léiriú i "
"réigiúin éagsúla den speictream leictreamaighnéadach. Tugtar banda ar gach "
"réigiún sa speictream. Úsáideann comhshuíomh fíordhatha bandaí solais "
"infheicthe dearg, glas agus gorm sna cainéil dhatha chomhfhreagracha dearg, "
"glas agus gorm, rud a fhágann táirge datha nádúrtha, a léiríonn an Domhan "
"go maith mar a d'fheicfeadh daoine go nádúrtha é.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"

msgid ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"The colours of natural waters differ markedly across the globe, depending "
"on water composition and illumination conditions. Ocean colour instruments "
"measure water-leaving radiance in narrow spectral bands to retrieve "
"water-quality indicators. The true colour of natural waters is derived by "
"calculating tristimulus values — the three primaries (X, Y, Z) that specify "
"a colour stimulus as perceived by the human eye.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."
msgstr ""
"# Tríspreagadh\n"
"\n"
"Bíonn dathanna uiscí nádúrtha an-éagsúil ar fud an domhain, ag brath ar "
"chomhdhéanamh an uisce agus ar choinníollacha soilsithe. Tomhaiseann "
"ionstraimí datha aigéin radaíocht a fhágann an t-uisce i mbandaí "
"speictreacha caola chun táscairí cáilíochta uisce a aisghabháil. "
"Díorthaítear fíordhath uiscí nádúrtha trí luachanna tríspreagtha a ríomh — "
"na trí phríomhdhath (X, Y, Z) a shonraíonn spreagadh datha mar a fheiceann "
"súil an duine é.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B05 (510 nm, cyan-green), and B02 (412.5 nm, violet) into "
"the red, green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a "
"near-infrared band used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it "
"in the red channel makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red "
"while water remains dark. B05 is sensitive to chlorophyll, sediment, "
"turbidity, and red tide, and B02 captures yellow dissolved organic matter "
"(CDOM) and detrital pigments. The composite is useful for ocean colour "
"analysis, coastal water quality monitoring, and distinguishing turbid or "
"sediment-laden waters from clear ocean.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"Mapálann an comhshuíomh datha bhréagaigh seo bandaí Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 "
"(865 nm, gar-infridheirg), B05 (510 nm, cian-ghlas), agus B02 (412.5 nm, "
"violait) isteach sna cainéil taispeána dearg, glas, agus gorm faoi seach. "
"Is banda gar-infridheirg é B17 a úsáidtear le haghaidh ceartú aeróisil agus "
"atmaisféir; nuair a chuirtear sa chainéal dearg é, bíonn plandúlacht agus "
"dromchlaí talún le feiceáil i ndearg geal agus fanann an t-uisce dorcha. Tá "
"B05 íogair do chlóraifil, dríodar, doiléireacht, agus taoide dhearg, agus "
"gabhann B02 ábhar orgánach tuaslagtha buí (CDOM) agus pigmintí "
"díthríotacha. Tá an comhshuíomh úsáideach d'anailís datha aigéin, "
"monatóireacht cáilíochta uisce cósta, agus uiscí doiléire nó "
"dríodair-ualaithe a idirdhealú ó aigéan glan.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B06 (560 nm, green), and B03 (442.5 nm, blue) into the red, "
"green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a near-infrared band "
"used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it in the red channel "
"makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red while water remains "
"dark. B06 is the chlorophyll absorption minimum reference band, and B03 "
"captures chlorophyll absorption and biogeochemical properties. Compared to "
"the B17/B05/B02 composite, the shifted green and blue channels offer a "
"different sensitivity to phytoplankton and dissolved organic matter in "
"coastal and open ocean waters.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"Mapálann an comhshuíomh datha bhréagaigh seo bandaí Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 "
"(865 nm, gar-infridheirg), B06 (560 nm, glas), agus B03 (442.5 nm, gorm) "
"isteach sna cainéil taispeána dearg, glas, agus gorm faoi seach. Is banda "
"gar-infridheirg é B17 a úsáidtear le haghaidh ceartú aeróisil agus "
"atmaisféir; nuair a chuirtear sa chainéal dearg é, bíonn plandúlacht agus "
"dromchlaí talún le feiceáil i ndearg geal agus fanann an t-uisce dorcha. Is "
"é B06 an banda tagartha íosmhéid ionsúcháin clóraifille, agus gabhann B03 "
"ionsú clóraifille agus airíonna bithgheocheimiceacha. I gcomparáid leis an "
"gcomhshuíomh B17/B05/B02, tugann na cainéil ghlas agus ghorm aistrithe "
"íogaireacht dhifriúil do fhíteaplanctón agus d'ábhar orgánach tuaslagtha in "
"uiscí cósta agus aigéin oscailte.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to "
"even out the exposure. It makes clouds look natural and keep as much visual "
"information as possible. Sentinel-3 OLCI tiles cover large areas, making it "
"possible to observe large cloud formations, such as hurricanes.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú Fíordhatha Feabhsaithe\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an script seo optamú buaicphointí chun picteilíní dóite a "
"sheachaint agus chun an nochtadh a chothromú. Fágann sé go mbíonn scamaill "
"le feiceáil go nádúrtha agus go gcoinníonn sé an oiread faisnéise amhairc "
"agus is féidir. Clúdaíonn tíleanna Sentinel-3 OLCI limistéir mhóra, rud a "
"fhágann gur féidir foirmíochtaí móra scamall, mar hairicíní, a bhreathnú.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"

msgid ""
"# Pansharpened True Color\n"
"\n"
"The pansharpened true color composite is done by using the usual true color "
"data (red, green and blue (RGB)) and enhancing them by using the "
"panchromatic band 8, or pan band (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). An image "
"from the pan band is similar to black-and-white film: it combines light "
"from the red, green, and blue parts of the spectrum into a single measure "
"of overall visible reflectance. Pansharpened images have 4x the resolution "
"of the usual true color composite, greatly enhancing the usefulness of "
"Landsat imagery.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."
msgstr ""
"# Fíordhath géaraithe le pan\n"
"\n"
"Déantar an comhshuíomh fíordhatha géaraithe le pan trí na sonraí fíordhatha "
"is gnách (dearg, glas agus gorm (RGB)) a úsáid agus iad a fheabhsú ag úsáid "
"banda painchrómatach 8, nó banda pan (is réigiún den speictream "
"leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le braiteoir satailíte an Domhan a "
"léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla). Tá íomhá ón mbanda pan cosúil le scannán "
"dubh-agus-bán: comhcheanglaíonn sé solas ó chodanna dearga, glasa agus "
"gorma den speictream isteach i dtomhas amháin ar fhrithchaitheacht "
"infheicthe iomlán. Tá 4x taifeach an chomhshuímh fíordhatha is gnách ag "
"íomhánna géaraithe le pan, rud a mhéadaíonn go mór úsáideacht íomhánna "
"Landsat.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."

msgid ""
"# False Color Urban composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite is used to visualise urbanized areas more clearly. "
"Vegetation is visible in shades of green, while urbanized areas are "
"represented by white, grey, or purple. Soils, sand, and minerals are shown "
"in a variety of colors. Snow and ice appear as dark blue, and water as "
"black or blue. Flooded areas are very dark blue and almost black. The "
"composite is useful for detecting wildfires and calderas of volcanoes, as "
"they are displayed in shades of red and yellow.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) and [here.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh Uirbeach Datha Bhréagaigh\n"
"\n"
"Úsáidtear an comhshuíomh seo chun limistéir uirbithe a amharcléiriú níos "
"soiléire. Bíonn plandúlacht le feiceáil i scáileanna glasa, agus léirítear "
"limistéir uirbithe i mbán, i liath, nó i gcorcra. Taispeántar ithreacha, "
"gaineamh, agus mianraí i ndathanna éagsúla. Bíonn sneachta agus oighear le "
"feiceáil mar ghorm dorcha, agus uisce mar dhubh nó gorm. Bíonn limistéir "
"thuilte gorm an-dorcha agus beagnach dubh. Tá an comhshuíomh úsáideach chun "
"tinte fiáine agus calderaí bolcán a bhrath, mar go dtaispeántar iad i "
"scáileanna dearga agus buí.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-"
"urban-rgb/) agus [anseo.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Agriculture composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared, near-infrared and blue bands to "
"monitor crop health (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Both short-wave and "
"near infrared bands are particularly good at highlighting dense vegetation, "
"which appears dark green in the composite. Crops appear in a vibrant green "
"and bare earth appears magenta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) and "
"[here.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh talmhaíochta\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an comhshuíomh seo bandaí infridhearg gearrthonnach, "
"gar-infridheirg agus gorm chun sláinte barr a mhonatóiriú (is réigiún den "
"speictream leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le braiteoir satailíte "
"an Domhan a léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla). Tá bandaí infridhearg gearrthonnach "
"agus gar-infridheirg araon go maith chun plandúlacht dhlúth a aibhsiú, a "
"bhíonn le feiceáil glas dorcha sa chomhshuíomh. Bíonn barra le feiceáil i "
"nglas bríomhar agus bíonn talamh lom le feiceáil mar mhaigeanta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais [anseo](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) agus "
"[anseo.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"

msgid ""
"# Snow Classifier\n"
"\n"
"The Snow Classifier algorithm aims to detect snow by classifying pixels "
"based on different brightness and Normalized Difference Snow Index (NDSI) "
"thresholds. Values classified as snow are returned in bright vivid blue. "
"The script can overestimate snow areas over clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"
msgstr ""
"# Aicmitheoir Sneachta\n"
"\n"
"Tá sé mar aidhm ag an algartam Aicmitheoir Sneachta sneachta a bhrath trí "
"phicteilíní a aicmiú bunaithe ar thairseacha gile agus Innéacs Difríochta "
"Normalaithe Sneachta (NDSI) éagsúla. Tugtar luachanna a aicmítear mar "
"shneachta ar ais i ngorm geal bríomhar. Is féidir leis an script limistéir "
"sneachta thar scamaill a mheas thar fóir.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/"
")"

msgid ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"The script aims to dynamically visualise the chlorophyll and sediment "
"conditions of water bodies, which are primary indicators of water quality. "
"The chlorophyll content ranges in colors from dark blue (low chlorophyll "
"content) through green to red (high chlorophyll content). Sediment "
"concentrations are colored brown; opaque brown indicates high sediment "
"content.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"
msgstr ""
"# Amharcóir Cáilíochta Uisce Ulyssys (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"Tá sé mar aidhm ag an script coinníollacha clóraifille agus dríodair "
"comhlachtaí uisce, atá ar na príomhtháscairí ar cháilíocht uisce, a "
"amharcléiriú go dinimiciúil. Bíonn ábhar clóraifille idir dathanna gorm "
"dorcha (ábhar íseal clóraifille) trí ghlas go dearg (ábhar ard "
"clóraifille). Bíonn tiúchan dríodair daite donn; léiríonn donn teimhneach "
"ábhar ard dríodair.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"

msgid ""
"# Short wave infrared composite (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Short wave infrared (SWIR) measurements can help scientists estimate how "
"much water is present in plants and soil, as water absorbs SWIR "
"wavelengths. Short wave infrared bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) are also useful for distinguishing between cloud types (water clouds "
"versus ice clouds), snow and ice, all of which appear white in visible "
"light. In this composite vegetation appears in shades of green, soils and "
"built-up areas are in various shades of brown, and water appears black. "
"Newly burned land reflects strongly in SWIR bands, making them valuable for "
"mapping fire damages. Each rock type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh infridhearg gearrthonnach (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir le tomhais infridhearg gearrthonnach (SWIR) cabhrú le heolaithe "
"measúnú a dhéanamh ar an méid uisce atá i bplandaí agus in ithir, mar go "
"n-ionsúnn uisce tonnfhaid SWIR. Tá bandaí infridhearg gearrthonnach (is "
"réigiún den speictream leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le braiteoir "
"satailíte an Domhan a léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla) úsáideach freisin chun "
"idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir cineálacha scamall (scamaill uisce i gcomparáid "
"le scamaill oighir), sneachta agus oighear, a bhíonn bán go léir i solas "
"infheicthe. Sa chomhshuíomh seo bíonn plandúlacht le feiceáil i scáileanna "
"glasa, bíonn ithreacha agus limistéir thógtha i scáileanna éagsúla donna, "
"agus bíonn uisce le feiceáil dubh. Frithchaitheann talamh a dódh le déanaí "
"go láidir i mbandaí SWIR, rud a fhágann go bhfuil siad luachmhar chun "
"damáiste tine a mhapáil. Frithchaitheann gach cineál carraige solas "
"infridhearg gearrthonnach go difriúil, rud a fhágann gur féidir geolaíocht "
"a mhapáil trí sholas SWIR frithchaite a chomparáid.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The Sentinel-2 normalised difference snow index can be used to "
"differentiate between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the "
"short-wave infrared light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is "
"generally reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in "
"bright vivid blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Sneachta (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir an t-innéacs difríochta normalaithe sneachta Sentinel-2 a úsáid "
"chun idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir clúdach scamall agus sneachta mar go "
"n-ionsúnn sneachta sa solas infridhearg gearrthonnach, ach go "
"bhfrithchaitheann sé an solas infheicthe, ach is gnách go mbíonn scamall "
"frithchaiteach sa dá thonnfhad. Léirítear clúdach sneachta i ngorm geal "
"bríomhar.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalised difference snow index (NDSI) can be used to differentiate "
"between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the short-wave infrared "
"light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is generally "
"reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in bright vivid "
"blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Sneachta (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir an t-innéacs difríochta normalaithe sneachta (NDSI) a úsáid chun "
"idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir clúdach scamall agus sneachta mar go n-ionsúnn "
"sneachta sa solas infridhearg gearrthonnach, ach go bhfrithchaitheann sé an "
"solas infheicthe, ach is gnách go mbíonn scamall frithchaiteach sa dá "
"thonnfhad. Léirítear clúdach sneachta i ngorm geal bríomhar.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Highlight Optimized Natural Color\n"
"\n"
"This script aims to display the Earth in beautiful natural color images. It "
"uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to even out the "
"exposure.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Dath Nádúrtha Optamaithe do Bhuaicphointí\n"
"\n"
"Tá sé mar aidhm ag an script seo an Domhan a thaispeáint in íomhánna áille "
"datha nádúrtha. Úsáideann sé optamú buaicphointí chun picteilíní dóite a "
"sheachaint agus chun an nochtadh a chothromú.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 12, 8, 2 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared (SWIR) band 12 to differentiate "
"among different rock types (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Each rock "
"and mineral type reflects short-wave infrared light differently, making it "
"possible to map out geology by comparing reflected SWIR light. Near "
"infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation and band 2 detects moisture, "
"both contributing to differentiation of ground materials. The composite is "
"useful for finding geological formations and features (e.g. faults, "
"fractures), lithology (e.g. granite, basalt, etc.) and mining applications.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh Geolaíochta 12, 8, 2\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an comhshuíomh seo banda 12 infridhearg gearrthonnach (SWIR) chun "
"idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir cineálacha éagsúla carraige (is réigiún den "
"speictream leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le braiteoir satailíte "
"an Domhan a léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla). Frithchaitheann gach cineál carraige "
"agus mianraí solas infridhearg gearrthonnach go difriúil, rud a fhágann gur "
"féidir geolaíocht a mhapáil trí sholas SWIR frithchaite a chomparáid. "
"Aibhsíonn banda 8 gar-infridheirg (NIR) plandúlacht agus braitheann banda 2 "
"taise, agus cuireann an dá cheann le difreáil ábhar talún. Tá an "
"comhshuíomh úsáideach chun foirmíochtaí agus gnéithe geolaíocha (m.sh. "
"fabhtanna, scoilteanna), litheolaíocht (m.sh. eibhear, basalt, srl.) agus "
"feidhmeanna mianadóireachta a aimsiú.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-"
"SWIR.pdf)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 8, 11, 12 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses both short-wave infrared (SWIR) bands 11 and 12 to "
"differentiate among different rock types (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). Each rock and mineral type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light. Near Infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation, contributing "
"to differentiation of ground materials. Vegetation in the composite appears "
"red. The composite is useful for differentiating vegetation, and land "
"especially geologic features that can be useful for mining and mineral "
"exploration.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh Geolaíochta 8, 11, 12\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an comhshuíomh seo bandaí 11 agus 12 infridhearg gearrthonnach "
"(SWIR) araon chun idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir cineálacha éagsúla carraige "
"(is réigiún den speictream leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le "
"braiteoir satailíte an Domhan a léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla). Frithchaitheann "
"gach cineál carraige agus mianraí solas infridhearg gearrthonnach go "
"difriúil, rud a fhágann gur féidir geolaíocht a mhapáil trí sholas SWIR "
"frithchaite a chomparáid. Aibhsíonn banda 8 gar-infridheirg (NIR) "
"plandúlacht, rud a chuireann le difreáil ábhar talún. Bíonn plandúlacht sa "
"chomhshuíomh le feiceáil i ndearg. Tá an comhshuíomh úsáideach chun "
"plandúlacht agus talamh a idirdhealú, go háirithe gnéithe geolaíocha a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith úsáideach don mhianadóireacht agus do thaiscéalaíocht "
"mianraí.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, visualizes wildfires using "
"Sentinel-2 data. It combines natural color background with some NIR/SWIR "
"data for smoke penetration and more detail, while adding highlights from "
"B11 and B12 to show fires in red and orange colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"
msgstr ""
"# Tinte fiáine\n"
"\n"
"Amharcléiríonn an script seo, a chruthaigh Pierre Markuse, tinte fiáine ag "
"úsáid sonraí Sentinel-2. Comhcheanglaíonn sé cúlra datha nádúrtha le roinnt "
"sonraí NIR/SWIR le haghaidh treá deataigh agus tuilleadh sonraí, agus "
"aibhsithe ó B11 agus B12 á gcur leis chun tinte a thaispeáint i ndathanna "
"dearga agus oráiste.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, based on the Pierre Markuse wildfire script, detects and "
"visualizes wildfires using Landsat 8/9 thermal and visible bands. It "
"combines natural color (B2, B3, B4) with thermal band (B10) analysis to "
"detect temperature anomalies and create a red-orange-white glow effect "
"highlighting fire locations.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/"
"main/landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"
msgstr ""
"# Tinte fiáine\n"
"\n"
"Braitheann agus amharcléiríonn an script seo, atá bunaithe ar script tinte "
"fiáine Pierre Markuse, tinte fiáine ag úsáid bandaí teirmeacha agus "
"infheicthe Landsat 8/9. Comhcheanglaíonn sé dath nádúrtha (B2, B3, B4) le "
"anailís banda teirmeach (B10) chun neamhrialtachtaí teochta a bhrath agus "
"éifeacht lonrach dhearg-oráiste-bhán a chruthú a aibhsíonn suíomhanna "
"tinte.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/"
"main/landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, uses multiple bands (a band is a "
"region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth "
"in different bands) and saturation and brightness control to enhance the "
"true color visualization.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Fíordhath Feabhsaithe\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an script seo, a chruthaigh Pierre Markuse, bandaí iolracha (is "
"réigiún den speictream leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le braiteoir "
"satailíte an Domhan a léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla) agus rialú sáithiúcháin "
"agus gile chun an t-amharcléiriú fíordhatha a fheabhsú.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"

msgid ""
"# Burned Area Index\n"
"\n"
"Burned Area Index takes advantage of the wider spectrum of Visible, "
"Red-Edge, NIR and SWIR bands.\n"
"\n"
"Values description:()=> The range of values for the index is `-1` to `1` "
"for burn scars, and `1` - `6` for active fires. Different fire intensities "
"may result in different thresholds; the current values were calibrated, as "
"per original author, on mostly Mediterranen regions.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Limistéir Dóite\n"
"\n"
"Baineann an tInnéacs Limistéir Dóite leas as speictream níos leithne de "
"bhandaí Infheicthe, Faobhar Dearg, NIR agus SWIR.\n"
"\n"
"Cur síos ar luachanna:()=> Is é `-1` go `1` raon luachanna an innéacs do "
"choilm dhóite, agus `1` - `6` do thinte gníomhacha. D'fhéadfadh tairseacha "
"difriúla a bheith mar thoradh ar dhéine tine éagsúla; calabraíodh na "
"luachanna reatha, de réir an bhunúdair, ar réigiúin Mheánmhuirí den chuid "
"is mó.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Burn Ratio is frequently used to estimate burn severity. It uses "
"near-infrared (NIR) and shortwave-infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. Healthy "
"vegetation has a high reflectance in the near-infrared portion of the "
"spectrum, and a low short-wave infrared reflectance. On the other hand, "
"burned areas have a high shortwave infrared reflectance but low reflectance "
"in the near infrared Darker pixels indicate burned areas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"nbr/)."
msgstr ""
"# Cóimheas Dóite Normalaithe (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Úsáidtear an Cóimheas Dóite Normalaithe go minic chun déine dóite a mheas. "
"Úsáideann sé tonnfhaid gar-infridheirg (NIR) agus infridhearg gearrthonnach "
"(SWIR). Bíonn frithchaitheacht ard ag plandúlacht shláintiúil i gcuid "
"gar-infridheirg den speictream, agus frithchaitheacht íseal infridhearg "
"gearrthonnach. Os a choinne sin, bíonn frithchaitheacht ard infridhearg "
"gearrthonnach ag limistéir dóite ach frithchaitheacht íseal "
"gar-infridheirg. Léiríonn picteilíní níos dorcha limistéir dóite.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"nbr/)."

msgid ""
"# Atmospheric penetration\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses different bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) in the non-visible part of the electromagnetic spectrum to reduce "
"the influence of the atmosphere in the image. Short wave infrared bands 11 "
"and 12 are highly reflected by the heated areas, making them useful for "
"fire and burned area mapping. Near infrared band 8, is on contrary, highly "
"reflected by vegetation, which signifies absence of fire. Vegetation "
"appears blue, displaying details related to the vegetation vigor. Healthy "
"vegetation is shown in light blue while the stressed, sparse or/and arid "
"vegetation appears in dull blue. Urban features are white, grey, cyan or "
"purple.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"
msgstr ""
"# Treá atmaisféir\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an comhshuíomh seo bandaí éagsúla (is réigiún den speictream "
"leictreamaighnéadach é banda; is féidir le braiteoir satailíte an Domhan a "
"léiriú i mbandaí éagsúla) sa chuid neamh-infheicthe den speictream "
"leictreamaighnéadach chun tionchar an atmaisféir san íomhá a laghdú. "
"Frithchaitheann na limistéir the bandaí 11 agus 12 infridhearg "
"gearrthonnach go mór, rud a fhágann go bhfuil siad úsáideach chun tine agus "
"limistéir dóite a mhapáil. Os a choinne sin, frithchaitheann plandúlacht "
"banda 8 gar-infridheirg go mór, rud a chiallaíonn nach bhfuil tine ann. "
"Bíonn plandúlacht le feiceáil gorm, ag taispeáint sonraí a bhaineann le "
"bríomhaireacht na plandúlachta. Taispeántar plandúlacht shláintiúil i ngorm "
"éadrom agus bíonn plandúlacht struis, tanaí nó/agus thirim le feiceáil i "
"ngorm maol. Bíonn gnéithe uirbeacha bán, liath, cian nó corcra.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais [anseo.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"

msgid ""
"# Barren Soil Visualization\n"
"\n"
"The Barren Soil Visualization can be useful for soil mapping, to "
"investigate the location of landslides or the extent of erosion in "
"non-vegetated areas. This visualization shows all vegetation in green and "
"the barren ground in red. Water appears black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) and "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú Ithreach Loim\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir leis an Amharcléiriú Ithreach Loim a bheith úsáideach chun "
"ithreacha a mhapáil, chun suíomh sciorrthaí talún nó méid an chreimthe i "
"limistéir gan plandúlacht a imscrúdú. Taispeánann an t-amharcléiriú seo "
"gach plandúlacht i nglas agus an talamh lom i ndearg. Bíonn uisce le "
"feiceáil dubh.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) "
"agus "
"[anseo.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"

msgid ""
"# True Color with IR Highlights composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite enhances the true color visualization by adding the "
"shortwave infrared wavelengths to amplify details. It displays heated areas "
"in red/orange.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-"
"9d1de0133733)"
msgstr ""
"# Comhshuíomh Fíordhatha le Buaicphointí IR\n"
"\n"
"Feabhsaíonn an comhshuíomh seo an t-amharcléiriú fíordhatha trí thonnfhaid "
"infridhearg gearrthonnach a chur leis chun sonraí a mhéadú. Taispeánann sé "
"limistéir the i ndearg/oráiste.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-"
"space-9d1de0133733)"

msgid ""
"# Detection of Burned Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script is used to detect large scale recently burned areas. Pixels "
"colored red highlight burned areas, and all other pixels are returned in "
"true color. The script sometimes overestimates burned areas over water and "
"clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"
msgstr ""
"# Brath Limistéar Dóite\n"
"\n"
"Úsáidtear an script seo chun limistéir mhóra a dódh le déanaí a bhrath. "
"Aibhsíonn picteilíní daite dearg limistéir dóite, agus tugtar gach "
"picteilín eile ar ais i bhfíordhath. Uaireanta déanann an script limistéir "
"dóite thar uisce agus scamaill a mheas thar fóir.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"

msgid ""
"# Scene classification\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Scene classification was developed to distinguish between cloudy pixels, "
"clear pixels and water pixels of Sentinel-2 data and is a result of ESA's "
"Scene classification algorithm. Twelve different classifications are "
"provided including classes of clouds, vegetation, soils/desert, water and "
"snow. It does not constitute a land cover classification map in a strict "
"sense.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."
msgstr ""
"# Aicmiú radharcanna\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Forbraíodh aicmiú radharcanna chun idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir picteilíní "
"scamallacha, picteilíní soiléire agus picteilíní uisce de shonraí "
"Sentinel-2 agus is toradh é ar algartam Aicmithe Radharcanna ESA. "
"Soláthraítear dhá aicmiú dhéag éagsúla lena n-áirítear aicmí scamall, "
"plandúlachta, ithreacha/fásaigh, uisce agus sneachta. Ní léarscáil aicmithe "
"clúdaigh talún é i gciall docht.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."

msgid ""
"# Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI) is estimated based on the "
"chlorophyll content in terrestrial vegetation and can be used to monitor "
"vegetation condition and health. Low OTCI values usually signify water, "
"sand or snow. Extremely high values, displayed with white, usually suggest "
"the absence of chlorophyll as well. They generally represent either bare "
"ground, rock or clouds. The chlorophyll values in between range from red "
"(low chlorophyll values) to dark green (high chlorophyll values) can be "
"used to determine vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Clóraifille Talúntaí (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Meastar an tInnéacs Clóraifille Talúntaí (OTCI) bunaithe ar ábhar "
"clóraifille i bplandúlacht thalúntach agus is féidir é a úsáid chun riocht "
"agus sláinte plandúlachta a mhonatóiriú. Is gnách go léiríonn luachanna "
"ísle OTCI uisce, gaineamh nó sneachta. Is gnách go moltar le luachanna "
"an-ard, a thaispeántar i mbán, nach bhfuil clóraifil ann ach an oiread. Is "
"gnách go léiríonn siad talamh lom, carraig nó scamaill. Is féidir na "
"luachanna clóraifille idir dearg (luachanna ísle clóraifille) agus glas "
"dorcha (luachanna arda clóraifille) a úsáid chun sláinte plandúlachta a "
"chinneadh.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"

msgid ""
"# Topographic Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a visualisation with green colours representing lowland "
"elevations and earth colours as mountainous elevations. The script uses "
"discrete classes rather than the continuous visualisations in the other DEM "
"layers.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú Topagrafach\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tugann an script seo amharcléiriú ar ais le dathanna glasa ag léiriú airde "
"talún ísle agus dathanna talún mar airde sléibhtiúil. Úsáideann an script "
"aicmí scoite seachas na hamharcléiriúcháin leanúnacha sna cisil DEM eile.\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir íosluachanna agus uasluachanna saincheaptha a shocrú san "
"evalscript trí defaultVis a shocrú ar false agus na hathróga min agus max a "
"shocrú ar na luachanna atá ag teastáil.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"

msgid ""
"# Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a color visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú Datha\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tugann an script seo amharcléiriú datha de mhúnla digiteach airde ar ais, "
"ag sannadh dathanna leanúnacha do theorainneacha na hairde.\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir íosluachanna agus uasluachanna saincheaptha a shocrú san "
"evalscript trí defaultVis a shocrú ar false agus na hathróga min agus max a "
"shocrú ar na luachanna atá ag teastáil.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Grayscale Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a grayscale visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú Griscála\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tugann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de mhúnla digiteach airde ar "
"ais, ag sannadh dathanna leanúnacha do theorainneacha na hairde.\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir íosluachanna agus uasluachanna saincheaptha a shocrú san "
"evalscript trí defaultVis a shocrú ar false agus na hathróga min agus max a "
"shocrú ar na luachanna atá ag teastáil.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"

msgid ""
"# Sepia Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a sepia visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú Seipia\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tugann an script seo amharcléiriú seipia de mhúnla digiteach airde ar ais, "
"ag sannadh dathanna leanúnacha do theorainneacha na hairde.\n"
"\n"
"Is féidir íosluachanna agus uasluachanna saincheaptha a shocrú san "
"evalscript trí defaultVis a shocrú ar false agus na hathróga min agus max a "
"shocrú ar na luachanna atá ag teastáil.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It displays water areas in blue (partially black) and "
"land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban areas are displayed in a "
"light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas in mustard green and "
"bare ground in a darker green.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. In order not to confuse "
"cryogenic features with non-cryogenic ones, some general information about "
"the location is helpful in interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú feabhsaithe\n"
"\n"
"Comhcheanglaíonn an script seo gamma0 na bpolarúchán VV agus VH in "
"amharcléiriú datha bhréagaigh. Taispeánann sé limistéir uisce i ngorm (dubh "
"go páirteach) agus talamh i scáileanna éagsúla buí/glas. Taispeántar "
"limistéir uirbeacha i nglas-bhuí éadrom (i dtreo bán), limistéir "
"phlandaithe i nglas mustaird agus talamh lom i nglas níos dorcha.\n"
"\n"
"I limistéir shneachta agus oighir, is féidir leis an amharcléiriú a bheith "
"éagsúil ó ghlas-bhuí éadrom thar ghlas níos gile go donn dorcha nó fiú "
"dubh. Chun gan gnéithe crióigineacha a mheascadh le gnéithe "
"neamh-chrióigineacha, tá roinnt faisnéise ginearálta faoin suíomh úsáideach "
"chun an íomhá a léirmhíniú."

msgid ""
"# SAR False Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations of "
"Sentinel-1 SAR data into a false color visualization. Water areas appear in "
"blue (partially black) and land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban "
"areas are displayed in light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas "
"in mustard green, and bare ground in darker green. The visualization "
"supports a wide range of monitoring applications, including ice and ship "
"tracking, agriculture and deforestation monitoring, and emergency response "
"scenarios such as flood and volcano observation.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. Some general knowledge of "
"the location is helpful to avoid confusing cryogenic features with other "
"land cover types.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Amharcléiriú Datha Bhréagaigh SAR\n"
"\n"
"Comhcheanglaíonn an script seo gamma0 na bpolarúchán VV agus VH de shonraí "
"SAR Sentinel-1 in amharcléiriú datha bhréagaigh. Bíonn limistéir uisce le "
"feiceáil i ngorm (dubh go páirteach) agus talamh i scáileanna éagsúla "
"buí/glas. Taispeántar limistéir uirbeacha i nglas-bhuí éadrom (i dtreo "
"bán), limistéir phlandaithe i nglas mustaird, agus talamh lom i nglas níos "
"dorcha. Tacaíonn an t-amharcléiriú le raon leathan feidhmeanna "
"monatóireachta, lena n-áirítear rianú oighir agus long, monatóireacht "
"talmhaíochta agus dífhoraoisithe, agus cásanna práinnfhreagartha amhail "
"breathnú ar thuilte agus bolcáin.\n"
"\n"
"I limistéir shneachta agus oighir, is féidir leis an amharcléiriú a bheith "
"éagsúil ó ghlas-bhuí éadrom thar ghlas níos gile go donn dorcha nó fiú "
"dubh. Tá roinnt eolais ghinearálta ar an suíomh úsáideach chun gan gnéithe "
"crióigineacha a mheascadh le cineálacha eile clúdaigh talún.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# Urban Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script uses Sentinel-1 SAR VH and VV polarisations to highlight urban "
"areas and buildings. Structures appear in different colours depending on "
"their backscatter characteristics: purple indicates high VH reflectance, "
"green indicates high VV reflectance, and white indicates high reflectance "
"in both. The red channel is restricted to pixels where VH exceeds 0.5, "
"helping separate buildings from bare soil. The script is useful for "
"monitoring urban expansion, assessing building density, and identifying "
"structures in flood-prone areas. Note that in mountainous terrain, steep "
"slopes and snow can produce similar signals, making it difficult to "
"separate urban areas from other features.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# Limistéir Uirbeacha\n"
"\n"
"Úsáideann an script seo polarúcháin VH agus VV SAR Sentinel-1 chun "
"limistéir uirbeacha agus foirgnimh a aibhsiú. Bíonn struchtúir le feiceáil "
"i ndathanna éagsúla ag brath ar a gcaractaristicí ais-scaipthe: léiríonn "
"corcra frithchaitheacht ard VH, léiríonn glas frithchaitheacht ard VV, agus "
"léiríonn bán frithchaitheacht ard sa dá cheann. Tá an cainéal dearg "
"teoranta do phicteilíní ina sáraíonn VH 0.5, rud a chabhraíonn le foirgnimh "
"a scaradh ó ithir lom. Tá an script úsáideach chun méadú uirbeach a "
"mhonatóiriú, dlús foirgneamh a mheas, agus struchtúir a aithint i limistéir "
"atá so-ghabhálach do thuilte. Tabhair faoi deara i dtír-raon sléibhtiúil "
"gur féidir le fánaí géara agus sneachta comharthaí comhchosúla a "
"tháirgeadh, rud a fhágann go bhfuil sé deacair limistéir uirbeacha a "
"scaradh ó ghnéithe eile.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# SAR Deforestation Detection\n"
"\n"
"This script processes Sentinel-1 VV and VH polarisation bands to detect "
"deforestation and forest degradation. It converts the backscatter values "
"into polar form to derive vector length and angle, which discriminate "
"between water, forest, and bare soil. Water and bare soil appear black, "
"forested areas are rendered in green gradients, and degraded or cleared "
"areas appear in red — with stronger colours indicating higher "
"classification confidence. The script is useful for monitoring forest loss "
"and land-use change over time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_deforestation_"
"detection/)."
msgstr ""
"# Brath Dífhoraoisithe SAR\n"
"\n"
"Próiseálann an script seo bandaí polarúcháin VV agus VH Sentinel-1 chun "
"dífhoraoisiú agus díghrádú foraoise a bhrath. Athraíonn sé na luachanna "
"ais-scaipthe go foirm pholach chun fad veicteora agus uillinn a dhíorthú, a "
"idirdhealaíonn idir uisce, foraois, agus ithir lom. Bíonn uisce agus ithir "
"lom le feiceáil dubh, rindreáiltear limistéir fhoraoisithe i ngrádáin "
"ghlasa, agus bíonn limistéir dhíghrádaithe nó imréitithe le feiceáil i "
"ndearg — le dathanna níos láidre ag léiriú muiníne aicmithe níos airde. Tá "
"an script úsáideach chun caillteanas foraoise agus athrú úsáide talún a "
"mhonatóiriú le himeacht ama.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_"
"deforestation_detection/)."

msgid ""
"# Water Surface Roughness\n"
"\n"
"This script visualizes water surface roughness using Sentinel-1 SAR data. "
"SAR backscatter is highly sensitive to the roughness of the water surface: "
"calm water reflects radar energy away from the sensor and appears dark, "
"while rough or wind-driven water scatters energy back and appears brighter. "
"Variations in surface roughness reveal oceanographic and maritime features "
"such as wind patterns, sea currents, internal waves, and ship wakes. Oil "
"spills dampen surface waves and appear as dark patches against the "
"surrounding rougher water. The visualization supports maritime monitoring "
"applications including ship tracking, oil pollution detection, and "
"observation of ocean circulation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Gairbhe Dromchla Uisce\n"
"\n"
"Amharcléiríonn an script seo gairbhe dromchla uisce ag úsáid sonraí SAR "
"Sentinel-1. Tá ais-scaipeadh SAR an-íogair do ghairbhe dhromchla an uisce: "
"frithchaitheann uisce ciúin fuinneamh radair ar shiúl ón mbraiteoir agus "
"bíonn sé le feiceáil dorcha, agus scaipeann uisce garbh nó "
"gaoithe-thiomáinte fuinneamh ar ais agus bíonn sé le feiceáil níos gile. "
"Nochtann éagsúlachtaí i ngairbhe dromchla gnéithe aigéanagrafaíochta agus "
"muirí amhail patrúin ghaoithe, sruthanna farraige, tonnta inmheánacha, agus "
"eireabaill long. Maolaíonn doirteadh ola tonnta dromchla agus bíonn siad le "
"feiceáil mar chlocha dorcha i gcoinne an uisce níos gairbhe máguaird. "
"Tacaíonn an t-amharcléiriú le feidhmeanna monatóireachta muirí lena "
"n-áirítear rianú long, brath truaillithe ola, agus breathnú ar chúrsaíocht "
"aigéin.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB ratio\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It uses the VV polarization in the red channel, the VH "
"polarization in the green channel, and a ratio of VH/VV in the blue "
"channel. It shows water areas in dark red (black), urban areas in yellow, "
"vegetated areas in turquoise, and bare ground in dark purple.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light yellow to "
"blue to red. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with non-cryogenic "
"ones, some general information about the location is helpful in "
"interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# Cóimheas RGB\n"
"\n"
"Comhcheanglaíonn an script seo gamma0 na bpolarúchán VV agus VH in "
"amharcléiriú datha bhréagaigh. Úsáideann sé an polarúchán VV sa chainéal "
"dearg, an polarúchán VH sa chainéal glas, agus cóimheas VH/VV sa chainéal "
"gorm. Taispeánann sé limistéir uisce i ndearg dorcha (dubh), limistéir "
"uirbeacha i mbuí, limistéir phlandaithe i dturcaid, agus talamh lom i "
"gcorcra dorcha.\n"
"\n"
"I limistéir shneachta agus oighir, is féidir leis an amharcléiriú a bheith "
"éagsúil ó bhuí éadrom go gorm go dearg. Chun gan gnéithe crióigineacha a "
"mheascadh le gnéithe neamh-chrióigineacha, tá roinnt faisnéise ginearálta "
"faoin suíomh úsáideach chun an íomhá a léirmhíniú."

msgid ""
"# SAR Urban\n"
"\n"
"The script is useful for locating urban areas and individual buildings. It "
"uses the gamma0 of the VH polarization and the VV polarizations to "
"highlight different buildings and topology orientations with purple and "
"green colors. It can be used to track urban expansion, estimate building "
"type, or locate buildings in risk areas (e.g., flooding).\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from white to purple to "
"dark blue or even black. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with "
"non-cryogenic ones, some general information about the location is helpful "
"to interpret the image. \n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR Uirbeach\n"
"\n"
"Tá an script úsáideach chun limistéir uirbeacha agus foirgnimh aonair a "
"aimsiú. Úsáideann sé gamma0 pholarúchán VH agus na polarúcháin VV chun "
"foirgnimh éagsúla agus treoshuímh topeolaíochta a aibhsiú le dathanna "
"corcra agus glasa. Is féidir é a úsáid chun méadú uirbeach a rianú, cineál "
"foirgnimh a mheas, nó foirgnimh a aimsiú i limistéir riosca (m.sh., "
"tuilte).\n"
"\n"
"I limistéir shneachta agus oighir, is féidir leis an amharcléiriú a bheith "
"éagsúil ó bhán go corcra go gorm dorcha nó fiú dubh. Chun gan gnéithe "
"crióigineacha a mheascadh le gnéithe neamh-chrióigineacha, tá roinnt "
"faisnéise ginearálta faoin suíomh úsáideach chun an íomhá a léirmhíniú. \n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# HH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships. It provides good contrast between water and "
"land surfaces. Compared to the linear gamma0 visualization, the decibel "
"gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HH - gamma0 deicibeil\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán HH. "
"Tá polarúchán HH níos lú íogair do ghairbhe dromchla i gcomparáid leis an "
"bpolarúchán VV agus dá bhrí sin úsáidtear é chun réada agus spriocanna crua "
"amhail longa a bhrath. Soláthraíonn sé codarsnacht mhaith idir dromchlaí "
"uisce agus talún. I gcomparáid leis an amharcléiriú gamma0 líneach, san "
"amharcléiriú gamma0 deicibeil tá scálú logartamach ar na sonraí."

msgid ""
"# HH - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships."
msgstr ""
"# HH - gamma0 líneach\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán HH. "
"Tá polarúchán HH níos lú íogair do ghairbhe dromchla i gcomparáid leis an "
"bpolarúchán VV agus dá bhrí sin úsáidtear é chun réada agus spriocanna crua "
"amhail longa a bhrath."

msgid ""
"# HV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HV "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (HV) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The HV "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization). Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HV - gamma0 deicibeil\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán HV. "
"Is gnách go mbíonn na luachanna don traspholarúchán (HV) níos ísle "
"(amharcléiriú níos dorcha) ná don chomhpholarúchán (HH, VV). Bíonn "
"luachanna níos airde ag an bpolarúchán HV do dhromchlaí arb iad is "
"saintréith dóibh scaipeadh toirte, m.sh., craobhacha, comhlachtaí ithreach "
"tirim, nó clúdaigh (dath níos éadroime san amharcléiriú) agus níos ísle do "
"dhromchlaí gan mórán scaipthe nó gan aon scaipeadh (dath níos dorcha san "
"amharcléiriú). I gcomparáid leis an amharcléiriú gamma0 líneach, san "
"amharcléiriú gamma0 deicibeil tá scálú logartamach ar na sonraí."

msgid ""
"# HV - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HV "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (HV) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The HV "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization)."
msgstr ""
"# HV - gamma0 líneach\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán HV. "
"Is gnách go mbíonn na luachanna don traspholarúchán (HV) níos ísle "
"(amharcléiriú níos dorcha) ná don chomhpholarúchán (HH, VV). Bíonn "
"luachanna níos airde ag an bpolarúchán HV do dhromchlaí arb iad is "
"saintréith dóibh scaipeadh toirte, m.sh., craobhacha, comhlachtaí ithreach "
"tirim, nó clúdaigh (dath níos éadroime san amharcléiriú) agus níos ísle do "
"dhromchlaí gan mórán scaipthe nó gan aon scaipeadh (dath níos dorcha san "
"amharcléiriú)."

msgid ""
"# VH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VH "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (VH) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The VH "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization). Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# VH - gamma0 deicibeil\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán VH. "
"Is gnách go mbíonn na luachanna don traspholarúchán (VH) níos ísle "
"(amharcléiriú níos dorcha) ná don chomhpholarúchán (HH, VV). Bíonn "
"luachanna níos airde ag an bpolarúchán VH do dhromchlaí arb iad is "
"saintréith dóibh scaipeadh toirte, m.sh., craobhacha, comhlachtaí ithreach "
"tirim, nó clúdaigh (dath níos éadroime san amharcléiriú) agus níos ísle do "
"dhromchlaí gan mórán scaipthe nó gan aon scaipeadh (dath níos dorcha san "
"amharcléiriú). I gcomparáid leis an amharcléiriú gamma0 líneach, san "
"amharcléiriú gamma0 deicibeil tá scálú logartamach ar na sonraí."

msgid ""
"# VH - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VH "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (VH) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV).  The VH "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization)."
msgstr ""
"# VH - gamma0 líneach\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán VH. "
"Is gnách go mbíonn na luachanna don traspholarúchán (VH) níos ísle "
"(amharcléiriú níos dorcha) ná don chomhpholarúchán (HH, VV).  Bíonn "
"luachanna níos airde ag an bpolarúchán VH do dhromchlaí arb iad is "
"saintréith dóibh scaipeadh toirte, m.sh., craobhacha, comhlachtaí ithreach "
"tirim, nó clúdaigh (dath níos éadroime san amharcléiriú) agus níos ísle do "
"dhromchlaí gan mórán scaipthe nó gan aon scaipeadh (dath níos dorcha san "
"amharcléiriú)."

msgid ""
"# VV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VV "
"polarization. Compared to the HH polarization, the VV polarization is more "
"sensitive to surface roughness and is therefore often used in the detection "
"of oil contamination or wake detection. Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# VV - gamma0 deicibeil\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán VV. I "
"gcomparáid leis an bpolarúchán HH, tá an polarúchán VV níos íogaire do "
"ghairbhe dromchla agus dá bhrí sin úsáidtear go minic é chun truailliú ola "
"nó eireabaill long a bhrath. I gcomparáid leis an amharcléiriú gamma0 "
"líneach, san amharcléiriú gamma0 deicibeil tá scálú logartamach ar na "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"# VV - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VV "
"polarization. Compared to the HH polarization, the VV polarization is more "
"sensitive to surface roughness and is therefore often used in the detection "
"of oil contamination or wake detection."
msgstr ""
"# VV - gamma0 líneach\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an script seo amharcléiriú griscála de gamma0 pholarúchán VV. I "
"gcomparáid leis an bpolarúchán HH, tá an polarúchán VV níos íogaire do "
"ghairbhe dromchla agus dá bhrí sin úsáidtear go minic é chun truailliú ola "
"nó eireabaill long a bhrath."

msgid ""
"# Total suspended matter concentration\n"
"\n"
"Satellite-derived total suspended matter (TSM) is a measure of the "
"concentration of particulate material in surface water such as mud, silt "
"and other fine-grainded sedimentss, including organic and inorganic "
"fractions. The TSM product is calculated based on the MERIS 1999 Baseline "
"Atmospheric Correction and the OCI neural net TSM algorithm by [Hieronymi "
"et al. "
"2017](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/"
"fmars.2017.00140/full). The product has variable accuracy and schould be "
"considert experimental.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/SentinelMissions/"
"Sentinel3.html#sentinel-3-olci-level-2)"
msgstr ""
"# Tiúchan iomlán ábhair ar fuaidreamh\n"
"\n"
"Is tomhas é an t-ábhar iomlán ar fuaidreamh (TSM) díorthaithe ó shatailít "
"ar thiúchan ábhair cáithníneach in uisce dromchla amhail láib, sil agus "
"dríodair mhíne eile, lena n-áirítear codanna orgánacha agus neamhorgánacha. "
"Ríomhtar an táirge TSM bunaithe ar Cheartú Atmaisféir Bunlíne MERIS 1999 "
"agus ar algartam líonra néaraigh OCI TSM le [Hieronymi et al. "
"2017](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/"
"fmars.2017.00140/full). Tá cruinneas inathraithe ag an táirge agus ba "
"cheart é a mheas turgnamhach.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/"
"SentinelMissions/Sentinel3.html#sentinel-3-olci-level-2)"

msgid ""
"# Aerosol optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"Aerosol optical thickness (AOT) is a measure of the extent to which "
"aerosols in the atmosphere prevent the transmission of light through "
"absorption and scattering. Optical thickness, also knwon as optical depth "
"depends on the physical nature, the shape and the concentration of "
"particles. AOT is often used in climatology and atmospheric research to "
"assess the effects of aerosols on weather, climate, and air quality.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"
msgstr ""
"# Tiús optúil aeróisil\n"
"\n"
"Is tomhas é tiús optúil aeróisil (AOT) ar an méid a gcuireann aeróisil san "
"atmaisféar bac ar tharchur solais trí ionsú agus scaipeadh. Braitheann tiús "
"optúil, ar a dtugtar doimhneacht optúil freisin, ar nádúr fisiciúil, ar "
"chruth agus ar thiúchan cáithníní. Úsáidtear AOT go minic i aeráideolaíocht "
"agus i dtaighde atmaisféir chun éifeachtaí aeróisil ar aimsir, aeráid, agus "
"cáilíocht aeir a mheas.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"

msgid ""
"# Photosynthetically active radiation\n"
"\n"
"The Photosynthetically Active Radiation (PAR) visualization displays the "
"instantaneous PAR at the water surface. It was adopted from FERIS and "
"developed based on an algorithm by [Aiken and Moore "
"(1997)](https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/documents/20142/37627/MERIS_ATBD_2.1"
"8_v4.0+-+1997+-+PAR.pdf/07a8cd54-94ba-4efe-fe9a-751d1ffc9381). The PAR is a "
"measure of the energy flux from the sun in the wavelenght range of 400–700 "
"nm. It is often used to convert measured chlorophyll concentration into an "
"estimate of ocen productivity and from this an estimate of the carbon "
"sequestration. As such, it plays an important role in modelling of the "
"carbon-cycle.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Radaíocht fhótasintéiseach ghníomhach\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an t-amharcléiriú Radaíochta Fótasintéisí Gníomhaí (PAR) an PAR "
"toirneach ag dromchla an uisce. Glacadh é ó FERIS agus forbraíodh é "
"bunaithe ar algartam le [Aiken agus Moore "
"(1997)](https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/documents/20142/37627/MERIS_ATBD_2.1"
"8_v4.0+-+1997+-+PAR.pdf/07a8cd54-94ba-4efe-fe9a-751d1ffc9381). Is tomhas é "
"an PAR ar shreabhadh fuinnimh ón ngrian sa raon tonnfhaid 400–700 nm. "
"Úsáidtear go minic é chun tiúchan clóraifille tomhaiste a thiontú ina "
"mheastachán ar tháirgiúlacht aigéin agus uaidh sin ina mheastachán ar "
"urghabháil carbóin. Dá bhrí sin, tá ról tábhachtach aige i múnlú an "
"timthrialla charbóin.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Diffuse attenuation coefficient\n"
"\n"
"The diffuse attenuation coefficient at 490 nm is a measure of how the "
"intensity of light decreases as it passes through a column of water. It "
"quantifies the rate at which light is absorbed and scattered by water and "
"its constituents, such as phytoplankton, dissolved organic matter and "
"suspended particles. This coefficient is crucial for understanding "
"underwater light environments and is widely used in marine biology, "
"oceanography and environmental science. It's calculated as described in "
"[Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Comhéifeacht mhaolaithe idirleata\n"
"\n"
"Is tomhas é an chomhéifeacht mhaolaithe idirleata ag 490 nm ar an gcaoi a "
"laghdaíonn déine solais agus é ag dul trí cholún uisce. Cainníonn sé an "
"ráta ar a n-ionsúitear agus ar a scaiptear solas ag uisce agus a "
"chomhpháirteanna, amhail fíteaplanctón, ábhar orgánach tuaslagtha agus "
"cáithníní ar fuaidreamh. Tá an chomhéifeacht seo ríthábhachtach chun "
"timpeallachtaí solais faoi uisce a thuiscint agus úsáidtear go forleathan í "
"sa bhitheolaíocht mhuirí, san aigéanagrafaíocht agus san eolaíocht "
"chomhshaoil. Ríomhtar í mar a thuairiscítear in [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307).\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Integrated water vapour column\n"
"\n"
"The integrated water vapour column displays the water vapour integrated "
"over an atmosphere column. It is displayed in kg/m2 and calculated on the "
"basis of band 18 (885 nm) and band 19 (900 nm). The product shows an "
"overestimation in the transition zones between glint and off-glint and has "
"a systematic overestimation of about 20%.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."
msgstr ""
"# Colún comhtháite gaile uisce\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an colún comhtháite gaile uisce an gal uisce comhtháite thar "
"cholún atmaisféir. Taispeántar é i kg/m2 agus ríomhtar é ar bhonn banda 18 "
"(885 nm) agus banda 19 (900 nm). Léiríonn an táirge ró-mheastachán sna "
"criosanna aistrithe idir limistéir frithchaithimh gréine (glint) agus "
"limistéir lasmuigh díobh agus tá ró-mheastachán córasach de thart ar 20% "
"ann.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."

msgid ""
"# Algal pigment concentration (open waters)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) developed by [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) and CI developed by [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Tiúchan pigmint algaí (uiscí oscailte)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) arna fhorbairt ag [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) agus CI arna fhorbairt ag [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Algal pigment concentration (complex waters)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) developed by [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) and CI developed by [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Tiúchan pigmint algaí (uiscí casta)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) arna fhorbairt ag [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) agus CI arna fhorbairt ag [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# CDM absorption coefficient\n"
"\n"
"The Coloured Detrital and Dissolved Material (CDM) absorption coefficient "
"at 443 nm indicates the fraction of incident light that is absorbed by both "
"detrital particles and colored dissolved organic matter (CDOM). Dissolved "
"organic matter is an important component of the oceanic carbon cycle. It is "
"also used as an indicator for assessing the impact of terrigenous inputs in "
"coastal waters.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/b2c93f4d-7d90-448f-a6f4-62f78e3"
"b673b)."
msgstr ""
"# Comhéifeacht ionsúcháin CDM\n"
"\n"
"Tugann comhéifeacht ionsúcháin an Ábhair Dhíthríotaigh agus Thuaslagtha "
"Dhaite (CDM) ag 443 nm le fios an codán den solas teagmhasach a ionsúitear "
"ag cáithníní díthríotacha agus ag ábhar orgánach tuaslagtha daite (CDOM) "
"araon. Is comhpháirt thábhachtach de thimthriall carbóin an aigéin é ábhar "
"orgánach tuaslagtha. Úsáidtear é freisin mar tháscaire chun tionchar "
"ionchuir thalúntacha a mheas in uiscí cósta.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/b2c93f4d-7d90-448f-a6f4-62f78"
"e3b673b)."

msgid ""
"# Aerosol Angstrom exponent\n"
"\n"
"The Aerosol Angstrom exponent is a parameter that describes how the optical "
"thickness of aerosols in the atmosphere varies with wavelength. It provides "
"information about the size distribution of aerosol particles, with higher "
"values indicating smaller particles and lower values indicating larger "
"particles. This exponent is often used in atmospheric research and "
"climatology to analyse the properties of aerosols and their effects on "
"climate and air quality.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"
msgstr ""
"# Easpónant Angstrom aeróisil\n"
"\n"
"Is paraiméadar é an t-easpónant Angstrom aeróisil a thuairiscíonn conas a "
"athraíonn tiús optúil aeróisil san atmaisféar de réir tonnfhad. "
"Soláthraíonn sé faisnéis faoi dháileadh méide cáithníní aeróisil, agus "
"luachanna níos airde ag léiriú cáithníní níos lú agus luachanna níos ísle "
"ag léiriú cáithníní níos mó. Úsáidtear an t-easpónant seo go minic i "
"dtaighde atmaisféir agus in aeráideolaíocht chun airíonna aeróisil agus a "
"n-éifeachtaí ar aeráid agus ar cháilíocht aeir a anailísiú.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"

msgid ""
"# Rectified reflectance 779\n"
"\n"
"The rectified reflectance product is a by-product of the GIFAPAR product. "
"It shows a virtual reflectance that is largely free of atmospheric and "
"angular effects and is a good approcimation of the top of the canopy "
"reflectances. The rectified reflectance 779 is based on the NIR band (band "
"17) with a wavelength of 779 nm.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."
msgstr ""
"# Frithchaitheacht cheartaithe 779\n"
"\n"
"Is fotháirge den táirge GIFAPAR é an táirge frithchaitheachta ceartaithe. "
"Taispeánann sé frithchaitheacht fhíorúil atá saor den chuid is mó ó "
"éifeachtaí atmaisféir agus uilleacha agus is neasachán maith é ar "
"fhrithchaitheachtaí bharr an chlúdaigh. Tá an fhrithchaitheacht cheartaithe "
"779 bunaithe ar an mbanda NIR (banda 17) le tonnfhad 779 nm.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."

msgid ""
"# Rectified reflectance 681\n"
"\n"
"The rectified reflectance product is a by-product of the GIFAPAR product. "
"It shows a virtual reflectance that is largely free of atmospheric and "
"angular effects and is a good approcimation of the top of the canopy "
"reflectances. The rectified reflectance 681 is based on the red band (band "
"10) with a wavelength of 681 nm.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."
msgstr ""
"# Frithchaitheacht cheartaithe 681\n"
"\n"
"Is fotháirge den táirge GIFAPAR é an táirge frithchaitheachta ceartaithe. "
"Taispeánann sé frithchaitheacht fhíorúil atá saor den chuid is mó ó "
"éifeachtaí atmaisféir agus uilleacha agus is neasachán maith é ar "
"fhrithchaitheachtaí bharr an chlúdaigh. Tá an fhrithchaitheacht cheartaithe "
"681 bunaithe ar an mbanda dearg (banda 10) le tonnfhad 681 nm.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."

msgid ""
"# Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"The Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR) is a bio-geophysical product used to study the "
"photosynthetic process of plants and is often used in diagnostic and "
"predictive models computing primary productivity of the vegetation "
"canopies. In addition, this parameter is also an input for the estimation "
"of assimilation of CO2 in vegetation. GIFAPAR ranges from 0–1.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."
msgstr ""
"# Codán Toirneach Glas de Radaíocht Fhótasintéiseach Infhaighte Ionsúite "
"(GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"Is táirge bithgheoifisiciúil é an Codán Toirneach Glas de Radaíocht "
"Fhótasintéiseach Infhaighte Ionsúite (GIFAPAR) a úsáidtear chun próiseas "
"fótasintéiseach plandaí a staidéar agus úsáidtear go minic é i múnlaí "
"diagnóiseacha agus tuartha a ríomhann táirgiúlacht phríomhúil clúdach "
"plandúlachta. Ina theannta sin, is ionchur é an paraiméadar seo freisin "
"chun ionchorprú CO2 i bplandúlacht a mheas. Tá GIFAPAR idir 0–1.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."

msgid ""
"# Integrated water vapour column\n"
"\n"
"The integrated water vapour column displays the water vapour integrated "
"over an atmosphere column. It is displayed in kg/m2 and calculated on the "
"basis of band 18 (885 nm) and band 19 (900 nm). The product provides stable "
"and high quality results, but shows a systematic overestimation of about "
"9%–13% copared to ground base reference.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."
msgstr ""
"# Colún comhtháite gaile uisce\n"
"\n"
"Taispeánann an colún comhtháite gaile uisce an gal uisce comhtháite thar "
"cholún atmaisféir. Taispeántar é i kg/m2 agus ríomhtar é ar bhonn banda 18 "
"(885 nm) agus banda 19 (900 nm). Soláthraíonn an táirge torthaí cobhsaí "
"ardcháilíochta, ach léiríonn sé ró-mheastachán córasach de thart ar 9%–13% "
"i gcomparáid le tagairt bhunaithe ar an talamh.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."

msgid ""
"# Land Surface Temperature (LST)\n"
"\n"
"The Land Surface Temperature (LST) product provides the temperature of the "
"Earth's surface as retrieved from the SLSTR thermal infrared channels. LST "
"is a key parameter in the physics of land surface, controlling the "
"partitioning of energy between the atmosphere and the land surface. It is "
"used in climate change monitoring, drought monitoring, and urban heat "
"island studies.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#S3-SLSTR-Products-"
"L2-LST-Products)."
msgstr ""
"# Teocht Dromchla Talún (LST)\n"
"\n"
"Soláthraíonn an táirge Teocht Dromchla Talún (LST) teocht dhromchla an "
"Domhain mar a aisghabhadh ó chainéil infridhearg teirmeacha SLSTR í. Is "
"paraiméadar tábhachtach í LST i bhfisic dhromchla na talún, a rialaíonn "
"deighilt an fhuinnimh idir an t-atmaisféar agus dromchla na talún. "
"Úsáidtear í i monatóireacht athraithe aeráide, monatóireacht triomaigh, "
"agus staidéir ar oileáin teasa uirbeacha.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#S3-SLSTR-"
"Products-L2-LST-Products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) is a dimensionless index "
"that describes the difference between visible and near-infrared reflectance "
"of vegetation cover. It can be used to estimate the density of vegetation "
"cover and monitor vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://github.com/eu-cdse/sentinel-hub-custom-scripts/tree/main/"
"sentinel-3/slstrl2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Innéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Plandúlachta (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Is innéacs gan toise é an tInnéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Plandúlachta "
"(NDVI) a chuireann síos ar an difríocht idir frithchaitheacht infheicthe "
"agus gar-infridheirg de chlúdach plandúlachta. Is féidir é a úsáid chun "
"dlús clúdaigh plandúlachta a mheas agus sláinte plandúlachta a mhonatóiriú.\n"
"\n"
"Tuilleadh eolais "
"[anseo](https://github.com/eu-cdse/sentinel-hub-custom-scripts/tree/main/"
"sentinel-3/slstrl2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"The Normalized Difference Vegetation Index is a spectral index indicating "
"the greenness of the vegetation."
msgstr ""
"Is innéacs speictreach é an tInnéacs Difríochta Normalaithe Plandúlachta a "
"thugann le fios glaise na plandúlachta."

msgid ""
"Number of clear-sky surface reflectance used for the inversion of the "
"bidirectional reflectance distribution function."
msgstr ""
"Líon na frithchaitheachta dromchla spéire soiléire a úsáidtear le haghaidh "
"inbhéartú fheidhm dháileadh na frithchaitheachta débhealaigh."

msgid ""
"Uncertainty of the NDVI is calculated by propagating the uncertainties "
"associated to the model parameters resulting from the inversion of the "
"bidirectional reflectance distribution function."
msgstr ""
"Ríomhtar éiginnteacht an NDVI trí na héiginnteachtaí a bhaineann le "
"paraiméadair an mhúnla a eascraíonn as inbhéartú fheidhm dháileadh na "
"frithchaitheachta débhealaigh a iomadú."

msgid "The Burn Scar layer indicates detected burn scars for a given day."
msgstr "Léiríonn an ciseal Colm Dóite coilm dhóite a braitheadh i gcás lae áirithe."

msgid "The Burn Scar layer indicates detected burn scars for a given month."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn an ciseal Colm Dóite coilm dhóite a braitheadh i gcás míosa "
"áirithe."

msgid "Fraction of pixel surface affected by fire at the day of the burn detection."
msgstr ""
"Codán de dhromchla an phicteilín a ndeachaigh tine i bhfeidhm air ar lá "
"bhrath an dóite."

msgid ""
"Fraction of pixel surface affected by fire at the month of the burn "
"detection."
msgstr ""
"Codán de dhromchla an phicteilín a ndeachaigh tine i bhfeidhm air i mí "
"bhrath an dóite."

msgid "Probability that the burn detection corresponds to an actual burn."
msgstr "Dóchúlacht go bhfreagraíonn brath an dóite do dhó iarbhír."

msgid "Day of burn in year (1-366), no burn (0) or flag (<0)."
msgstr "Lá an dóite sa bhliain (1-366), gan dó (0) nó bratach (<0)."

msgid "Probability that the fractional burned area is above 0.1."
msgstr "Dóchúlacht go bhfuil an limistéar dóite codánach os cionn 0.1."

msgid "Probability that the fractional burned area is above 0.1˝."
msgstr "Dóchúlacht go bhfuil an limistéar dóite codánach os cionn 0.1˝."

msgid ""
"DMP, or Dry Matter Productivity, represents the overall growth rate or dry "
"biomass increase of the vegetation, expressed in kilograms of dry matter "
"per hectare per day (kgDM/ha/day). DMP is directly related to NPP (Net "
"Primary Productivity, in gC/m²/day), but its units are customized for "
"agro-statistical purposes. "
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn DMP, nó Táirgiúlacht Ábhair Thirim, an ráta fáis iomlán nó an "
"méadú ar bhithmhais thirim na plandúlachta, arna chur in iúl i gcileagraim "
"ábhair thirim in aghaidh an heicteáir in aghaidh an lae (kgDM/ha/lá). Tá "
"DMP bainteach go díreach le NPP (Príomhtháirgiúlacht Ghlan, i gC/m²/lá), "
"ach tá a haonaid saincheaptha chun críocha agra-staidrimh. "

msgid ""
"FAPAR corresponds to the fraction of photosynthetically active radiation "
"absorbed by the green elements of the canopy. The FAPAR value results "
"directly from the radiative transfer model in the canopy which is computed "
"instantaneously. It depends on canopy structure, vegetation element optical "
"properties and illumination conditions. FAPAR is very useful as input to a "
"number of primary productivity models based on simple efficiency "
"considerations."
msgstr ""
"Freagraíonn FAPAR do chodán na radaíochta fótasintéisí gníomhaí a "
"ionsúitear ag eilimintí glasa an chlúdaigh. Eascraíonn luach FAPAR go "
"díreach ón múnla aistrithe raidiciúil sa chlúdach a ríomhtar láithreach. "
"Braitheann sé ar struchtúr an chlúdaigh, ar airíonna optúla eilimintí "
"plandúlachta agus ar choinníollacha soilsithe. Tá FAPAR an-úsáideach mar "
"ionchur do roinnt múnlaí príomhtháirgiúlachta bunaithe ar bhreithnithe "
"éifeachtúlachta simplí."

msgid ""
"FCover is defined as the fraction of ground surface covered by green "
"vegetation as seen from the nadir direction. It is used to separate "
"vegetation and soil in energy balance processes, including temperature and "
"evapotranspiration. It is computed from the leaf area index and other "
"canopy structural variables and does not depend on variables such as the "
"geometry of illumination as compared to FAPAR. For this reason, it is a "
"very good candidate for the replacement of classical vegetation indices for "
"the monitoring of green vegetation. Because of the linear relationship with "
"radiometric signal, FCover will be only marginally scale dependent. Note "
"that similarly to LAI and FAPAR, only the green elements will be "
"considered, either belonging both to the overstory and understory."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear FCover mar chodán dhromchla na talún atá clúdaithe ag "
"plandúlacht ghlas mar a fheictear ó threo an nadir é. Úsáidtear é chun "
"plandúlacht agus ithir a scaradh i bpróisis chothromaíochta fuinnimh, lena "
"n-áirítear teocht agus galú-trasghalú. Ríomhtar é ón innéacs achair "
"duilleoige agus athróga struchtúracha eile an chlúdaigh agus ní bhraitheann "
"sé ar athróga amhail geoiméadracht an tsoilsithe i gcomparáid le FAPAR. Ar "
"an gcúis seo, is iarrthóir an-mhaith é chun innéacsanna plandúlachta "
"clasaiceacha a ionadú le haghaidh monatóireachta ar phlandúlacht ghlas. Mar "
"gheall ar an gcaidreamh líneach leis an gcomhartha raidiméadrach, ní bheidh "
"FCover ach beagán spleách ar scála. Tabhair faoi deara, cosúil le LAI agus "
"FAPAR, nach gcuirfear san áireamh ach na heilimintí glasa, bídís ina gcuid "
"den cheannbhrat uachtarach nó den fhásra íochtarach."

msgid ""
"Gross Primary Production (GPP) expresses a component of Primary Production "
"of ecosystems related to the creation of new organic matter by vegetation. "
"GPP is the total amount of dry matter (carbon) \"fixed\" by land plants per "
"unit time through photosynthesis (atmospheric CO2 into organic compounds). "
"A substantial fraction of GPP supports plant autotrophic respiration (Ra). "
"GPP is typically expressed as gram of carbon per square meter per day "
"(gC/m2 /day)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Príomhtháirgeadh Comhlán (GPP) comhpháirt de Phríomhtháirgeadh "
"éiceachórais in iúl a bhaineann le cruthú ábhair orgánaigh nua ag "
"plandúlacht. Is é GPP an méid iomlán ábhair thirim (carbón) a “shocraíonn” "
"plandaí talún in aghaidh an aonaid ama trí fhótasintéis (CO2 atmaisféir ina "
"chomhdhúile orgánacha). Tacaíonn cuid shubstaintiúil de GPP le análú "
"autotrófach plandaí (Ra). Is gnách GPP a chur in iúl mar ghram carbóin in "
"aghaidh an mhéadair chearnaigh in aghaidh an lae (gC/m2 /lá)."

msgid ""
"LAI is defined as half the developed area of photosynthetically active "
"elements of the vegetation per unit horizontal ground area. It determines "
"the size of the interface for exchange of energy (including radiation) and "
"mass between the canopy and the atmosphere. This is an intrinsic canopy "
"primary variable that should not depend on observation conditions. LAI is "
"strongly non-linearly related to reflectance. Therefore, its estimation "
"from remote sensing observations is scale dependent."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear LAI mar leath de limistéar forbartha eilimintí "
"fótasintéiseacha gníomhacha na plandúlachta in aghaidh an aonaid achair "
"talún chothrománaigh. Cinneann sé méid an chomheadain chun fuinneamh (lena "
"n-áirítear radaíocht) agus mais a mhalartú idir an clúdach agus an "
"t-atmaisféar. Is príomhathróg intreach clúdaigh í seo nár chóir di brath ar "
"choinníollacha breathnóireachta. Tá LAI bainteach go neamhlíneach go láidir "
"le frithchaitheacht. Dá bhrí sin, braitheann a mheastachán ó bhreathnuithe "
"cianbhraite ar scála."

msgid ""
"LAI is defined as half the developed area of photosynthetically active "
"elements of the vegetation per unit horizontal ground area. It determines "
"the size of the interface for exchange of energy (including radiation) and "
"mass between the canopy and the atmosphere. This is an intrinsic canopy "
"primary variable that should not depend on observation conditions. LAI is "
"strongly non-linearly related to reflectance."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear LAI mar leath de limistéar forbartha eilimintí "
"fótasintéiseacha gníomhacha na plandúlachta in aghaidh an aonaid achair "
"talún chothrománaigh. Cinneann sé méid an chomheadain chun fuinneamh (lena "
"n-áirítear radaíocht) agus mais a mhalartú idir an clúdach agus an "
"t-atmaisféar. Is príomhathróg intreach clúdaigh í seo nár chóir di brath ar "
"choinníollacha breathnóireachta. Tá LAI bainteach go neamhlíneach go láidir "
"le frithchaitheacht."

msgid ""
"\"NPP, or Net Primary Production, is an indicator of the rate at which "
"plants produce net useful chemical energy expressed in mass of carbon per "
"unit area per day (gC/m²/day).\""
msgstr ""
"\"Is táscaire é NPP, nó Príomhtháirgeadh Glan, ar an ráta ar a dtáirgeann "
"plandaí fuinneamh ceimiceach úsáideach glan arna chur in iúl i mais carbóin "
"in aghaidh an aonaid achair in aghaidh an lae (gC/m²/lá).\""

msgid ""
"SWI computed with a characteristic time length of 1 day. The Soil Water "
"index (SWI) provides global daily information about moisture conditions in "
"different soil depths. Near Real Time Data uses the EUMETSAT ASCAT-25km SSM "
"product in orbit format as input data. The Archive of ASCAT SWI uses "
"reprocessed SSM data from TU Wien."
msgstr ""
"SWI arna ríomh le fad ama sainiúil de lá amháin. Soláthraíonn an tInnéacs "
"Uisce Ithreach (SWI) faisnéis dhomhanda laethúil faoi choinníollacha taise "
"i ndoimhneachtaí éagsúla ithreach. Úsáideann Sonraí Beagnach Fíor-Ama an "
"táirge EUMETSAT ASCAT-25km SSM i bhformáid orbite mar shonraí ionchuir. "
"Úsáideann Cartlann ASCAT SWI sonraí SSM athphróiseáilte ó TU Wien."

